  "limitations": [
    "V0.9 public qualification remains incomplete. Local on-chain safety exercises do not demonstrate ten-million ballot capacity or a fully qualified operational incident process.",
    "Fuzzing is time-bounded and covers the selected parsers/proofs; it is not a cryptographic or application audit.",
    "Windows abrupt-process tests cover SIGKILL/restart after a durable transaction, not electrical power loss or rollback of a host-controlled backup.",
    "The frozen context, recovery root and qualification reviewer policy must be authenticated independently of the evidence they verify.",
    "Physical operator separation, timing truth and deployment independence cannot be established from labels or signatures alone.",
    "The existing PWA and workshop retain their genesis and version 0.8 interface. Recovery roots were installed only in isolated PUBLIC_TEST_ONLY local exercises; no public deployment or emergency reserve activation was performed."
  ],
  "scope_choice": "Prepare and test locally; independent WAN infrastructure and external audits not yet available",
  "local_safety_decision": "spec/decisions/0016-suspensions-locales-v0.9.md"
}
